---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bluetooth / OpenPlod (experimental — packaging vs protocol)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Phase 6 publishes **host packaging** requirements only
(`docs/ble-host.md`, Compose/doctor refusals for in-container BLE). Default
Docker `core`/`cpu`/`gpu`/`mac` profiles do **not** support Bluetooth radio.

No OpenPlod / openplaud-derived **protocol or provision** code is required for
core packaging. When the Phase 4 BLE adapter is present in-tree:

- Preserve MIT notices for OpenPlod contributions.
- Keep openplaud provenance / licence attribution current in ATTRIBUTION.md.
- Do not redistribute Plaud SDK AAR binaries or trademarks.
- Treat CI `plaud-bridge` builds as compile evidence only — not transfer proof.

Until hardware acceptance on a declared OS, BLE remains experimental.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Private / reverse-engineered Plaud APIs
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Private or reverse-engineered Plaud session/API clients are permanently out of
scope for Plaud-local cloud sync. Official Open API (and official cloud MCP for
ingest) are the only supported cloud paths. Do not add clients derived from
Applaud, plaud-tools, plaud-toolkit, PlaudNotes, or similar private stacks.
